          "type": "intro",
          "title": "You Live Inside a Machine the Size of a Planet",
          "content": "Right now, a sunbeam is striking the Pacific. It is warming water that will, in eight days, evaporate into a cloud that will rain on Kansas wheat that will feed cattle that will exhale **CO₂** into an atmosphere that will heat back the very ocean that started this loop.\n\nThis is **Earth System Science** — the recognition that the **atmosphere**, **hydrosphere**, **lithosphere**, and **biosphere** are not separate subjects in different textbooks. They are one machine, exchanging energy and matter every second. Pull a thread anywhere — a forest, a glacier, a coral reef — and you tug something on the other side of the planet.\n\nThis lesson teaches you to **think in systems**. By the end, words like “feedback,” “reservoir,” and “energy budget” will become tools you actually use to read the news, your weather app, and your own backyard.",
