          "explanation": "**Soil organic carbon is in dynamic exchange with the atmosphere.** When soils are tilled, drained, or degraded, microbes break down organic matter and release CO₂. Conversely, restoring soils — through cover crops, no-till, agroforestry, regenerative grazing — sequesters carbon. The IPCC lists soil carbon storage among the highest-potential, **lowest-cost** natural climate solutions. Losing even 1% of global soil carbon would dwarf decades of fossil emissions.",
