          "explanation": "Oceans have **enormous thermal mass** — they warm slowly and cool slowly, moderating any climate downstream. SF's summer high stays in the 60s and winter low stays in the 40s because of the cold California Current and prevailing westerly winds. St. Louis, 1,500 miles inland, has nothing to buffer it — summer highs near 90°F, winter lows in the teens. **Latitude sets potential climate; geography sets actual climate.**",
