          "type": "application",
          "title": "Know Your Climate, Read Your Forecasts",
          "content": "Three habits to upgrade your climate literacy:\n\n1. **Look up your hometown's Köppen code.** Wikipedia or climate-data.org. Knowing you're Cfa vs Csb vs Dfb is climate literacy.\n\n2. **Find your local climate normal.** NOAA's NowData or local NWS office. Check current weather against that average. \"Today is 12°F above normal\" is a useful piece of context.\n\n3. **Track a Köppen migration story.** Pick a topic — French wine regions, Vermont maple syrup, California citrus, Arizona summer extremes. Once a year, search news for updates. You'll watch climate change live.",
