          "explanation": "**Wladimir Köppen** was a botanist before becoming a climatologist. He noticed that natural vegetation responds to climate **better than any single instrument record** — trees won't grow where it's too cold (warmest month < 10°C = treeline), grasslands replace forests where precipitation falls below ~40 cm, etc. His thresholds (the -3°C/18°C boundary for C/D, the 10°C boundary for E) match real botanical limits. This is why Köppen maps almost match biome maps.",
