          "type": "application",
          "title": "Become an Evidence Sleuth",
          "content": "Three habits to make this real:\n\n1. **Track one variable yourself.** Visit NASA GISS for monthly global temperatures or NOAA NCEI for the US records. Each month, glance at the anomaly. Build intuition for what \"+1.3°C above 1880-1980\" feels like in practice.\n\n2. **Watch one ice satellite story.** GRACE-FO mission live updates monthly Greenland and Antarctic mass. NASA has a free dashboard. Watching ice disappear in near-real-time is sobering and informative.\n\n3. **Cross-check one claim weekly.** Pick a climate-related news headline. Trace it back: which dataset? Which paper? What does the IPCC AR6 actually say about this topic? Five minutes of checking transforms you from a passive reader to a literate citizen.",
