          "explanation": "The \"global warming pause\" or \"hiatus\" was a real-but-misleading slowdown of **surface temperature** in the 2000s, driven by short-term ocean heat redistribution (the deep ocean kept warming). The starting point (1998) was a record El Niño that artificially inflated the trend's start. **Ocean heat content was unambiguous** — it accelerated throughout the alleged pause. By 2014 onwards, every year became warmer than 1998. Cherry-picking start dates is the **most common skeptical argument** — and one that convergence of evidence completely refutes.",
