          "explanation": "**Climate change is profoundly asymmetric.** Bangladesh emits 0.5 tons of CO₂ per person per year while facing existential sea-level rise and flooding. The US emits 15+ tons per person and is the largest cumulative emitter (25% of historical emissions). Without **climate justice** considerations — the **Loss and Damage fund** (COP27), tech transfer agreements, climate finance commitments — vulnerable nations have little incentive to join climate agreements that constrain their development while the historic polluters benefited. Justice is a **practical**, not just ethical, necessity.",
