          "explanation": "Lesson 1 framed Earth as **four reservoirs — geosphere, hydrosphere, atmosphere, biosphere — exchanging matter and energy continuously**. The carbon cycle moves carbon between rocks (geosphere), oceans (hydrosphere), air (atmosphere), and living things (biosphere) over short and long timescales. Lesson 2 added plate tectonics, which slowly reshapes the geosphere itself and drives long-term climate via volcanism, weathering, and continental arrangement. Climate change isn't a story about one reservoir — it's about how a perturbation to atmospheric CO₂ ripples through all four. \"Tightly coupled\" is the operative phrase: changes anywhere propagate everywhere.",
