          "explanation": "Lesson 4 showed how **oceans drive weather**: evaporation supplies atmospheric moisture, ocean currents (Gulf Stream, Kuroshio) redistribute equatorial heat poleward, and ENSO oscillations shift global weather patterns for years at a time. Lesson 6 added the **greenhouse-pace** dimension: oceans have absorbed roughly **90% of the excess heat** trapped by greenhouse gases since 1971, and around **30% of human CO₂ emissions** — that's why atmospheric warming has been slower than the radiative forcing alone would suggest. This ocean uptake also causes **acidification** (lower pH) and **stratification** (warm surface over cold deep), both of which damage marine ecosystems. The ocean is the climate's flywheel, buffer, and silent sink all at once.",
